<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Rights groups oppose UAE’s Lana Nusseibeh for UN chief over Sudan claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:022ce2746623e0b1ec0dd8115e4d3c6044036fb21e70df5e11e17d620d951644</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T02:56:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-lana-nusseibeh-un-chief-uae-sudan-rights-groups" /><summary type="html">Human rights groups on Tuesday urged countries to reject UAE diplomat Lana Nusseibeh’s bid to become UN secretary general citing allegations that Abu Dhabi funds Sudan’s paramilitary Rapid Support Forces. The UAE denies the accusations. Nusseibeh, 48, is seeking to become the first woman to lead the United Nations.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>King Charles confronts calls for slavery apology during Caribbean tour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbb2b47aec167109efc377eddf9aa0ba633d294e833398af3b031009909350c5</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T23:14:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-king-charles-slavery-apology-caribbean-tour" /><summary type="html">King Charles III began a Caribbean tour in the Bahamas on Tuesday, acknowledging “the great suffering of the past” amid calls for an apology over slavery. The 77-year-old monarch, undergoing cancer treatment, will also visit Guyana and Antigua and Barbuda, highlighting climate threats and attending a Commonwealth summit with Queen Camilla.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Israel election: Netanyahu and Eisenkot battle to form government after deadlock</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf236b8540180484cae56765d2f1057f273ab9fdb623b0d44331d0482da430f9</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T22:58:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-israel-election-record-turnout-netanyahu-eisenkot-deadlock" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and rival Gadi Eisenkot both pledged on Wednesday to form a government after an election left neither bloc with a parliamentary majority. Record voter turnout followed a divisive campaign dominated by the October 7, 2023 attack, while Arab Israeli parties made significant gains.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel: First exit polls show no clear winner, Arab parties make gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc730c3f265a231ce41b16c7f272db1749fe497d1de9e4d01b454425c5d09a8e</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T21:41:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-israel-first-exit-polls-show-no-clear-winner-arab-parties-make-gains" /><summary type="html">Exit polls on Tuesday showed that the opposition bloc led by Israeli opposition candidate Gadi Eisenkot gained a narrow edge over Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's Likud bloc in the Knesset. 
 
Likud, however, was projected to be the largest single party in the Israeli parliament.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bibi's moment of truth: Israel votes in first general election since October 7</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a315ac729055130a10b3c3fc18245eaea9b23f332c6a7dc13af0c62b7ba3835</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T21:26:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261027-bibi-s-moment-of-truth-israel-votes-in-first-general-election-since-october-7" /><summary type="html">The turnout tells the tale. Israelis casting ballots in their largest numbers in decades in the first general election since the October Seventh attacks of 2023. A referendum on the bloodiest day in the nation’s history? Definitely that. And more: What kind of Israel do citizens want?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Brazil's defeated candidate Flavio Bolsonaro heads to US, sources say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c3cddf4338b8ad234da40dbf94f8d535a7a5ad9c540dd671d1a1c2b970b5ea4</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T20:49:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-defeated-brazilian-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-passports-cancelled-whereabouts-unknown" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Live: Israeli exit polls show narrow edge for opposition but no clear majority against Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16229dbd777ad1ad20f4dd241db9fe6c9c6da03d6a6feeaa610be0cf51d84d69</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T20:16:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-live-polls-open-in-first-israeli-election-since-october-7-attack--7c2b87d7e0f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-live-polls-open-in-first-israeli-election-since-october-7-attack" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu govt has 'attacked' Israeli judicial system, Supreme Court and democratic institutions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c627f4c51ba6051d3584be942ad1db6d8b703d3529eb315537bb2f54aaa23f83</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T19:44:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-govt-has-attacked-israeli-judicial-system-supreme-court-and-democratic-institutions" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Alain Greilsammer, Professor of Political Science at Bar-Ilan University in Tel Aviv. In the wake of the October 7 attacks, regional tensions with Iran, and deepening domestic divisions, Greilsammer argues that the election will be fundamentally shaped by concerns over democratic accountability, judicial independence and the unequal distribution of civic obligations. He warns Netanyahu’s policies risk transforming Israel into “something like an authoritarian or non-democratic state.” He suggests that Israel’s Arab political parties could play a decisive role in determining the election’s outcome.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ibrahim Abu Ahmad on Israeli election: 'Crucial for Arab citizens to have ally in Jewish community'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b4e6a4c8bebf502127e844b510af8cf90280d37bf5044e53877752e83dc25c5</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T18:59:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-ibrahim-abu-ahmad-on-israeli-election-crucial-for-arab-citizens-to-have-ally-in-jewish-community" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Ibrahim Abu Ahmad, Author, Palestinian Israeli political and peace activist and Head of Social Media for Israel's left-wing Democrats. “Currently, the sentiment in Israel is built around fear and trauma,” explains Ahmad. His most striking observation concerns the apparent contradiction between political leadership and public sentiment: “Many want to see an Arab-Jewish coalition. It's the leadership that is afraid to say it.” Ultimately, he moves beyond conventional electoral calculations to frame Arab-Jewish partnership as a question of democratic survival.</summary></entry><entry><title>How student assemblies brought down the Serbian government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ee35103905af6a1fe961f464fc12e3bc013aacd87d90c67b0f16b8bc3f89e13</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T18:58:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261027-how-student-assemblies-brought-down-the-serbian-government" /><summary type="html">A list of academics, engineers, artists and activists chosen by Serbia’s student assemblies defeated long-ruling president Aleksandar Vucic's right-wing Serbian Progressive Party Sunday. The shock victory comes after nearly two years of student-led anti-corruption protests – and may serve as a model for other movements hoping to turn street demonstrations into concrete political change.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli elections a 'referendum' on Netanyahu, security and whether Israel will 'remain a democracy'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90cbb3434554ac48e279f44a8f7c5e84e6854839b07cf70c83e1757d6f1e0b4e</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T18:34:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-elections-a-referendum-on-netanyahu-security-and-whether-israel-will-remain-a-democracy" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Ron Gerlitz, CEO of aChord Center at Hebrew University, an Israeli organization specialising in the social psychology of intergroup relations. “The main issue in this election is the fight for Israeli democracy,” explains Gerlitz. And beneath the struggle over democratic institutions lies the erosion of Benjamin Netanyahu's longstanding association with national security. Gerlitz also examines the psychological foundations of Netanyahu's enduring support, the influence of conspiracy narratives, the electoral significance of Arab parties and the uncertain future of the two-state solution.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴Live: Israeli election committee refuses Netanyahu's request to extend voting hours</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f43f211ec9761ea31a4d81d78d3d9604a147b0d6ddec03641040f4b65be35f77</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T18:30:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-live-polls-open-in-first-israeli-election-since-october-7-attack--7c2b87d7e0f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-live-polls-open-in-first-israeli-election-since-october-7-attack" /></entry><entry><title>Rights groups say proposed French law to make rioters pay for damage is anti-democratic</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc3f5750c561a86747207f126b3386ab09ebfded96dfdb7477b29c663710baf1</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T18:27:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261027-rights-groups-say-proposed-french-law-to-make-rioters-pay-for-damage-anti-democratic" /><summary type="html">Critics have said that a proposed French law that would make rioters liable to pay thousands of euros for any damage they cause is anti-democratic, as it could undermine the legitimate right to protest. The government put forward the law in a bid to quell looting and vandalism on the fringes of ongoing national protests over poor conditions in French schools and the high cost of living.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>France: Lawmakers hold a minute of silence for Pengo Bossio Wangi, victim of racist attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c42942e7d6c2af921b5b977a2d97aa40b861d1d11c8ca0fe840d79592a83563</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T17:08:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-lawmakers-hold-a-minute-of-silence-for-pengo-bossio-wangi-victim-of-racist-attack-1" /><summary type="html">French lawmakers held a minute of silence for Pengo Bossio Wangi. The victim of a racist attack died in a shooting last week, while at least five other people were wounded, including a 12-years-old girl. FRANCE 24’s Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israelis vote in a tense election: What's at stake?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ecb9bf9c33c18aa4e20811830abc74b5cb846b646d5e2521c127ddda10c4172</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T16:59:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israelis-vote-in-a-tense-election-what-s-at-stake" /><summary type="html">Israelis were voting Tuesday (October 27) in a tense national election widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership since the Hamas-led Oct. 7, 2023, attack on Israel and the wars that have since shaken the Middle East.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel elections: voter turnout reaches 55% by 4pm local time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d12511a913915ba00c021072eba46395fe00d466e7d39acbe5dbe94993812d2</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T16:52:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-elections-voter-turnout-reaches-55-by-4pm-local-time" /><summary type="html">Israelis flocked to the polls Tuesday (October 27) in turnout unseen in decades, with a deeply divided electorate delivering a verdict on veteran right-wing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu in the first election since the October 7, 2023 attack. FRANCE24's Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil's defeated candidate Flavio Bolsonaro flees to US despite cancelled passports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eadfaeab0c0f01c732f0c5403ea5a4f802d37bbd300c1cce88e8db5a5a4819b8</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T16:33:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-defeated-brazilian-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-passports-cancelled-whereabouts-unknown" /><summary type="html">Brazil's former presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro fled to the US, sources said Tuesday, despite his passports being cancelled after he failed to comply with a Supreme Court order to hand them over as part of a money laundering probe. Bolsonaro's whereabouts had been a source of speculation since his election defeat on Sunday to leftist incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>USA: Could a Democrat win a statewide election in Texas?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d260f7c5669517a5ae11d4896bd8cfc38689be1cb42618f475b2cf8be61348c</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:47:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-usa-could-a-democrat-win-a-statewide-election-in-texas" /><summary type="html">There is only one week left until the US midterm elections. In Texas, Democratic candidate James Talarico, could win a Senate seat for the first time in decades.</summary></entry><entry><title>Africa's Ebola outbreak tops 10,000 cases, mainly in DR Congo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bd1976d249105a9faa7645f65501d5e0cca7532f983fa2a490aa9377c312949</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:45:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261027-africa-ebola-outbreak-tops-10-000-cases-mainly-dr-congo" /><summary type="html">Africa's outbreak of the Ebola virus has passed more than 10,000 cases, health authorities said Tuesday, with the vast majority located in Democratic Republic of Congo. There are currently no approved vaccines for the rare Bundibugyo species of Ebola driving the current infections.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Live: Netanyahu's party asks to extend Israeli election hours amid record turnout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9851b6a6948fa7d22d58bac8a8ce962902e4887aaffcf42f5cff519d62ec49ba</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:39:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-live-polls-open-in-first-israeli-election-since-october-7-attack--7c2b87d7e0f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-live-polls-open-in-first-israeli-election-since-october-7-attack" /></entry><entry><title>Israel votes in decisive election: What happens after polls close?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0727288a6032dafb29688c6dfbe8e2d308449777a9d6167f07472178c758070e</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:55:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-israel-s-unique-political-system-what-happens-after-polls-close" /><summary type="html">Israelis are voting in a pivotal election Tuesday (October 27) as their country wrestles with unresolved wars, continues to reel from Hamas' 2023 attack and is deeply divided over the character of the state and the right person to lead it. Details by FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor, Angela Diffley.</summary></entry><entry><title>Canadian dance-punk legend Peaches reaches the ripe age of 60</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bd82ddcdc6ca415aa4ea8afdba9b6ffd28e14e77e9aeff4b558e0b8d002211a</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:50:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261027-canadian-dance-punk-legend-peaches-reaches-the-ripe-age-of-60" /><summary type="html">Canadian electroclash artist Peaches has been delighting, amusing and shocking music lovers and festivalgoers for the past three decades. Her shows are also a safe space for all genders and sexualities, although less so if you are averse to crowd surfing, extravagant pubic wigs and body-augmenting costumes.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Turnout high as Israeli voters deliver verdict on Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa8f6c827916ff59ed9d1cf1d1dfbce71037c154a9492dc2922e8caa723a5329</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:45:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/turnout-high-as-israeli-voters-deliver-verdict-on-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israelis flocked to the polls Tuesday (October 27) in turnout unseen in decades, with a deeply divided electorate delivering a verdict on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu in the first election since the October 7, 2023 attack. Former FRANCE 24 correspondent, Irris Makler, tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel: Netanyahu supporters gather as PM votes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:320be7a6c97187c252ae25990fb8969f92e2f2fb6135e64ee4c352e3e0439ffb</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:37:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-netanyahu-supporters-gather-as-pm-votes--3f57cd1da13b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-netanyahu-supporters-gather-as-pm-votes" /><summary type="html">Supporters of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu gathered outside a polling station where the leader was voting on Tuesday. This is Israel's first election since the October7, 2023 Hamas attack and is seen as a referendum on Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry></feed>
